## Environment Variables

We strongly recommend passing secrets via environment variables rather than embedding them in `.tf` files:

```bash
export FABRIC_TENANT_ID="00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
export FABRIC_CLIENT_ID="11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
export FABRIC_CLIENT_SECRET="your-client-secret-value"
```

The provider also recognizes standard Azure SDK aliases (`AZURE_TENANT_ID`, `ARM_TENANT_ID`, `AZURE_CLIENT_ID`, `ARM_CLIENT_ID`, `AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `ARM_CLIENT_SECRET`).

## Tenant Permissions & Scopes

To manage item-level permissions (`fabricext_*_permission`) and OneLake Data Access Roles (`fabricext_lakehouse_data_access_role`), the Service Principal requires:

1. **Workspace Access**: **Admin** or **Member** role on the target workspace.
2. **Tenant Settings**: The tenant setting *"Service principals can use Fabric APIs"* enabled in Fabric Admin Portal under Developer settings.

If using `fabricext_item_share_gate` or `modules/permissions` with `verify_item_shares = true`, the provider queries the Microsoft Fabric Admin API (`GET /v1/admin/workspaces/{workspaceId}/items/{itemId}/users`). This additionally requires:

1. Fabric tenant setting *"Service principals can use Fabric admin APIs"* (or *"read-only admin APIs"*).
2. Microsoft Entra ID Application permission `Tenant.Read.All` or `Tenant.ReadWrite.All`.

~> **Note:** If `verify_item_shares = false`, Admin APIs are bypassed completely, avoiding any requirement for tenant admin roles.

## Regional Cluster Discovery

When authenticating as a Service Principal (`app-only` token posture), the provider automatically queries the Power BI REST gateway (`GET /v1.0/myorg/groups`) to discover regional backend cluster URIs via the `home-cluster-uri` response header. For interactive user identities (`delegated-user` posture), the provider uses the portal bootstrap endpoint.
